WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.452
Exercise 8: publish everything to Entropy Data.

2
00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:11.855
No cloud account? Run the Community Edition locally. The setup script creates account, organization, and API key.

3
00:00:11.905 --> 00:00:16.871
Check that the Entropy Data CLI can connect.

4
00:00:16.921 --> 00:00:35.203
Create the owning teams first. Contracts and products reference them.

5
00:00:35.254 --> 00:00:53.854
Publish your four data contracts.

6
00:00:53.904 --> 00:01:04.358
Publish both data products. Entropy Data reads ODPS natively.

7
00:01:04.408 --> 00:01:21.267
Connect them: SKU Sales consumes the orders_v2 port of Orders.

8
00:01:21.317 --> 00:01:31.634
Run the tests again and publish the results to the platform.

9
00:01:31.684 --> 00:01:38.031
In the platform, other teams can now find your data products.

10
00:01:38.081 --> 00:01:43.327
Orders: owner, purpose, tags, and support channel, straight from your ODPS file.

11
00:01:43.377 --> 00:01:50.820
The orders_v2 port: tests passed, one consumer. The retired v1 port is hidden.

12
00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:57.919
Open SKU Sales. The access agreement shows up as a link to Orders.

13
00:01:57.969 --> 00:02:05.937
Further down: purpose, owner, and the output port with its data contract.

14
00:02:05.987 --> 00:02:12.486
The contract page: schema, terms of use, and owner.

15
00:02:12.536 --> 00:02:18.279
Data Quality shows the test results you published.

16
00:02:18.329 --> 00:02:26.628
Every check of the last run, with its result.
